<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>Privacy and your PDF | Learn</title>
  <meta name="description" content="What happens to the PDF you upload to Learn: what is read, what is sent, what is kept and for how long.">
  <style>
    :root {
      color-scheme: light;
      --paper: #f7f8f2;
      --ink: #18352c;
      --muted: #52655b;
      --forest: #173d32;
      --forest-light: #285a47;
      --lime: #ddf58b;
      --line: #dce3d8;
      font-family: Inter, ui-sans-serif, system-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
    }
    * { box-sizing: border-box; }
    body { margin: 0; background: var(--paper); color: var(--ink); font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.65; }
    a { color: var(--forest-light); text-underline-offset: 4px; }
    :focus-visible { outline: 3px solid #7052b5; outline-offset: 4px; }
    main { max-width: 760px; margin: auto; padding: 22px 20px 64px; }
    .site-header { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 12px 20px; padding-bottom: 20px; margin-bottom: 32px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
    .brand { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; color: var(--ink); font-size: 20px; font-weight: 850; letter-spacing: -.6px; text-decoration: none; }
    .brand-mark { display: grid; place-items: center; width: 38px; height: 38px; border-radius: 13px; background: var(--forest); color: var(--lime); font-size: 22px; font-weight: 900; }
    .back { padding-block: 10px; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 750; }
    h1 { margin: 0 0 10px; font-size: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 2.75rem); font-weight: 850; letter-spacing: -.04em; line-height: 1.1; }
    .intro { margin: 0; color: var(--muted); font-size: 17px; }
    .summary { margin: 28px 0 8px; padding: 20px 24px; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 20px; background: white; }
    .summary h2 { margin-top: 0; }
    .summary ul { margin: 0; padding-left: 20px; }
    .summary li { margin: 6px 0; }
    h2 { margin: 34px 0 8px; font-size: 1.25rem; letter-spacing: -.02em; line-height: 1.3; }
    p { margin: 0 0 12px; }
    address { font-style: normal; line-height: 1.6; }
    .updated { margin-top: 36px; color: var(--muted); font-size: 14px; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
<main>
  <header class="site-header">
    <a class="brand" href="/"><span class="brand-mark" aria-hidden="true">L</span>Learn</a>
    <a class="back" href="/">← Back to study cards</a>
  </header>

  <h1>Privacy and your PDF</h1>
  <p class="intro">What happens to the PDF you upload, in plain words.</p>

  <section class="summary" aria-labelledby="short-title">
    <h2 id="short-title">The short version</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>No account and no sign-up. Learn sets no cookies.</li>
      <li>Your PDF is read on our server to make your cards. It isn't saved.</li>
      {% if ai_cards %}
      <li>To write Detective cards, the text of the pages you choose is sent to an AI model.</li>
      {% else %}
      <li>No AI model is used right now: your cards are made by Learn's own rules on our server.</li>
      {% endif %}
      <li>No ads and no tracking.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <h2>When you upload a PDF</h2>
  <p>Your PDF goes to our server, which runs on Render, over an encrypted connection (HTTPS). The server reads the text of the pages you choose, makes your cards and sends them back to your browser as a PDF. Uploads can be up to {{ max_mb }} MB.</p>
  <p>Your PDF and your cards aren't saved to disk or to a database, and there is no history of uploads. While a large upload is being read, the web server may hold it in a temporary file that is deleted when the request ends.</p>
  <p>If some pages are scanned pictures of text, the server reads them with Tesseract, a text-reading program that runs on the server itself. Nothing is sent to an outside service for this.</p>

  {% if ai_cards %}
  <h2>When AI writes your Detective cards</h2>
  <p>To write the clue cards, the text of the pages you choose is sent to {{ ai_service }}. The PDF file itself isn't sent, and nothing about you is sent with the text.</p>
  <p>The finished cards, not your PDF, stay in the server's memory for a short time, so previewing and then downloading the same PDF doesn't ask the AI twice. Only the {{ kept }} most recent are kept, and they are gone when the server restarts.</p>
  <p>Up to {{ daily_limit }} uploads a day get AI-written cards. After that, or if the AI can't be reached, you get basic Detective cards made on our server, with a note on the cards saying why.</p>
  {% else %}
  <h2>AI</h2>
  <p>The site isn't set up to use an AI model right now, so the text of your PDF stays on our server.</p>
  {% endif %}

  <h2>Logs</h2>
  <p>Like most web servers, ours logs each request: the page asked for, the network address it came from, and when.{% if ai_cards %} For each Detective upload it also notes how many cards the AI wrote, which model it used, how many requests and tokens that took, and how long.{% endif %} Your PDF and its text are not in the logs.</p>

  <h2>The Study Visual Library</h2>
  <p>Pictures in the <a href="/library">library</a> load straight from Wikimedia Commons, so your browser contacts Wikimedia when you open that page.</p>

  <h2>Who Learn is for</h2>
  <p>Learn is for parents and students aged 18 and over. Younger students: ask a parent to upload your notes.</p>

  <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
  <p>Learn is run by {{ contact.name }}. For a question about your data, or anything else, email <a href="mailto:{{ contact.email }}">{{ contact.email }}</a> or write to:</p>
  <address>{{ contact.name }}<br>{% for line in contact.address %}{{ line }}<br>{% endfor %}</address>

  <p class="updated">Last updated 24 October 2026.</p>
</main>
</body>
</html>
